From 92b7b813f3e9cf56829c8038f604be09af69cf8f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HempFiend <17104973+jaidenscool1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 15:26:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 27/28] nx2: passthrough backend: sole mode decodes ASTC on the
 Vulkan device

In sole mode the Vulkan device is idle, and the CPU path (Eglantine's software ASTC decoder + stb BC
encode, six workers) finished only ~20-50 large textures a second in a race: a course's racers, Lakitu
and HUD pieces stayed black for seconds to minutes. 2D textures (and arrays) now go through the Vulkan
texture cache's own GPU transcode (astc_decoder.comp, then bc_encoder.comp), into a host-visible buffer
instead of an image (TextureCacheRuntime::TranscodeAstcForPassthrough; registered with the backend by
RasterizerVulkan in sole mode, Nx2Passthrough::SetGpuAstc). A worker checks a texture's opacity (BC1 when
opaque, else BC3), the entry thread hands checked textures to the GPU back thread (the scheduler's owner)
outside the backend's lock, at most 512 MiB of decode images at a time (EDEN_NX2_PASSTHROUGH_GPU_ASTC_MB),
one submission per batch; workers swizzle the returned blocks into the arena as before.

- The decoder reads the guest layout: ImageInfo::native_tiling must be the memory manager's, as the
  texture cache sets it (without it every other 8x8 block decoded black: median error 20 per channel).
  EDEN_NX2_PASSTHROUGH_GPU_ASTC_CHECK=<n> compares the first n against the CPU decoder: median 1.97,
  p90 4.6, worst 10.4 (BC1 quantization).
- A present can run on the GPU front in sole mode (a guest syncpoint action calls Composite) while the
  back records these batches: RendererVulkan::Composite takes Nx2Passthrough::VulkanMutex() in sole mode
  (without it: SIGSEGV in vkDestroyImageView, TickFrame and the batch recycling the same decode images).
- EDEN_NX2_PASSTHROUGH_GPU_ASTC=0 keeps the CPU path.

MKW, sole async: 37k textures decoded by the Vulkan device, 0 failed, from boot to the menus in ~40 s;
the race start frame has every racer, Lakitu, the HUD and the ground textured (before: black silhouettes
at the countdown). Racing ~12.5 fps either way (bounded by drains, not textures).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
